!!! 14-cross-language.matrix  --  page 1 of 3
!!!
!!! Matrix and Ny in one program. This page declares the shared types; the
!!! other two consume them.
!!!
!!! WHY THREE PAGES
!!!
!!! The obvious two-page arrangement -- a Matrix book and an Ny module that
!!! each use the other -- is a module dependency cycle, which Ny cannot order
!!! and reports as "Module dependency cycle detected among input files". So
!!! the dependency runs one way through a chain, and both directions of
!!! cross-language use are still demonstrated:
!!!
!!!     14-cross-language.matrix          book tour.mixed      (this page)
!!!         declares Measurement and Sampler
!!!              |
!!!              v
!!!     14-cross-language-helper.ny       module tour.ny_helper
!!!         Ny DERIVES from a Matrix class and CONSTRUCTS a Matrix record
!!!              |
!!!              v
!!!     14-cross-language-app.matrix      book tour.app
!!!         Matrix CALLS an Ny paragraph and USES an Ny class
!!!
!!! WHAT MAKES THIS WORK
!!!
!!! Not a translation layer. Both front ends emit the same NIL, carrying the
!!! same book::name storage identities, the same record and choice schemas,
!!! and the same class ancestry records. A Matrix book IS a NIL module, so an
!!! Ny import of it is an ordinary module import.
!!!
!!! The identity rules that make it hold are exact, and each was a real bug
!!! before it was a rule:
!!!   - a book path normalises '.' to '::', because Ny's module declaration
!!!     does; 'tour.mixed' and 'tour::mixed' are one module, and a Matrix book
!!!     that emitted dots produced schema names no Ny program could ever name;
!!!   - a declaration's spelling, with '-' rewritten to '_', is the emitted
!!!     NIL symbol, because Ny identifiers admit no hyphen and NIL identity is
!!!     case-significant;
!!!   - so an Ny client spells a Matrix name exactly as the Matrix page
!!!     declared it. Matrix-internal references fold case; cross-language ones
!!!     do not, and cannot, because Ny is case-sensitive.

book tour.mixed


!!! A record declared in Matrix. Its NIL schema is byte-identical to the
!!! equivalent Ny struct, so Ny code can construct it, pass it, store it in a
!!! field and raise it as a fault payload. 'matrix.execution' proves the
!!! schema equality against a hand-written Ny twin rather than asserting it.
public Measurement begin record
    field sensor  as text
    field reading as number
end record


!!! A class declared in Matrix. Ny code may derive from it, take an ancestor
!!! view of it, and dispatch virtually through it, because NIL's class section
!!! records ancestry and method declarations independently of which surface
!!! produced them.
!!!
!!! 'my' is the receiver here; Matrix synthesises the explicit first 'self'
!!! parameter Ny requires, so the CALL_METHOD arity matches a hand-written Ny
!!! method exactly.
public Sampler begin class
    field offset as number

    public virtual sample receives raw as number returns number begin paragraph
        give raw plus my offset
    end paragraph
end class
